<article class="detail">
  <h1>What is Object Biography?</h1>
  <div class="detail-text">
    <p>Every object has a history.</p>

    <p>Object Biography is an independent project exploring military artifacts and the people who used them.</p>

    <p>I&rsquo;ve collected militaria for over 30 years, with a particular interest in objects that retain a connection to their original owners. Through photographs, firsthand accounts, and historical research, I document the details and personal histories that might otherwise be lost.</p>

    <p>Not every story can be fully told, nor is every detail meant to be shared. My goal is to preserve what can be established, respect the people behind these objects, and share what makes them worth remembering.</p>

    <blockquote class="hero-quote page-footnote">
      <p>&ldquo;Biographies of things can make salient what might otherwise remain obscure.&rdquo;</p>
      <cite>&mdash; Igor Kopytoff, <em>The Cultural Biography of Things</em> (1986)</cite>
    </blockquote>
  </div>
</article>
